 ```
 
 | Subcommand | Flags / args | Description |
 |---|---|---|
 | `status` | `--json` | Print the local gdskills install status summary. |
 | `list` | `--json` | List registered project skills as a table. |
 | `inspect <project-skill>` | `--json` | Inspect one project skill: metadata + file presence. Missing target exits `1`. |
 | `route <query-or-target>` | `--json` | Score/rank registry entries against a free-text query or path. |
-| `resolve-context` | `--files <file>[,<file>...]` (required), `--for implement\|test\|review` (required), `--task-type <type>`, `--max-bytes <n>`, `--out <path>`, `--json` | Resolve, deterministically and project first, which rules, project skills and referenced project contracts an implementer, test writer or reviewer must read for the given files. Each entry carries `path`, `sha256`, `bytes`, `reason` (`glob:<g>`, `always`, `task-type:<t>`, `replaces-bundled`, `route`, `bundled-default`, `referenced-by:<path>`), `tier` (`must_read` or `on_demand`) and, for a project rule that replaces a bundled one, `shadows`. Project entries come first, bundled ones after; a bundled rule a project rule replaces is dropped. An `alwaysApply` rule above 30,720 bytes is listed as an `on_demand` index. `must_read` bytes are counted against the cap (`--max-bytes`, else `gdskills.projectContext.maxBytes` in `tasks.config.json`, default 131072); the remainder is listed `on_demand` and `budget.exceeded` is set with one stderr warning — rules are never cut and the exit code stays `0`. A link-mode rule is read from its origin only while its sha256 equals the registry's. `--out` must be inside the project. The last result is recorded in `.metaproject/data/skills/project-context/last.json`. A missing `--for` or `--files` exits `1`. |

